# llama.cpp (vendored copy)

A trimmed copy of llama.cpp, used by digiKam's natural language search feature
to run a local LLM for query interpretation. The source is vendored directly
rather than referenced as a git submodule, because KDE's git infrastructure
does not permit submodules. This follows the same approach as other bundled
third-party code in digiKam.

- Upstream project : https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
- Vendored version : tag b9859 (commit 4fc4ec5541b243957ae5099edb67372f8f3b550e)
- Vendored on      : 2026-07-07

## What was kept

Only the files required to build the library on CPU: src/, include/, ggml/,
common/, and the CMake build files. Upstream examples, tools, tests, CI
configuration, Python conversion scripts, language bindings, and documentation
were removed.

## Updating this vendored copy

When llama.cpp is upgraded:

1. Check out the desired tag from upstream and copy the same subset of
   directories (src/, include/, ggml/, common/, cmake/, CMakeLists.txt) over
   this copy.
2. Update llama_cpp_manifest.txt with the new snapshot date and git commit
   hash. This manifest is parsed at packaging time to populate the
   Help > Components Info dialog, so the exact embedded llama.cpp version is
   visible to users and in bug reports. It must be kept up to date manually.
3. Rebuild and verify SearchLlamaBackend still compiles - the llama.cpp API
   changes between versions.
